    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d951">

                <pb facs="0887" n="877" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg877"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/16670: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-06-06T12:00:00+07:00">June 6,
                            1941—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received June 7—12:01 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>224. During air raid on Chungking between hours of 7 and 11 on evening of June 5
                    Japanese planes also dropped bombs on south bank, one or more of which landed
                    about 400 yards behind Chancery while others hit sand bar on foreshore about 400
                    yards from residence occupied by members of Embassy staff causing slight damage
                    from fallen plaster.</p>
                <p>Sent to Department. Repeated to Shanghai, Peiping, Hankow. Shanghai please repeat
                    to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
